Skip "The only membership state included in a gapped incremental sync is for
senders in the timeline" for katrix.

The test asserts that a limited (gappy) incremental sync under
lazy_load_members returns only the timeline senders' membership events. That
expectation cannot be satisfied by any conforming homeserver: per the spec and
Synapse, a limited sync returns ALL state changes in the window
(StateFilter.all() when batch.limited) regardless of lazy-loading. Synapse
blacklists this exact test (riot-web#7211), and the sytest source itself marks
it "# XXX: N.B. THIS TEST IS DISABLED ATM AS WE HAVE DISABLED LL IN GAPPY
SYNCS".

It is SKIPPED (not blacklisted) so the run report counts it as SKIP rather
than FAIL: run-tests.pl skips a test whose requires contains a non-fixture
token missing from %proven ("lack of $req"), before any fixture runs. This
keeps the per-run diff detector honest — a skipped test is not a failing
signal.

If this stops applying against a newer sytest develop, rebase it (the hunk is
in stable, old test code).

--- a/tests/31sync/15lazy-members.pl
+++ b/tests/31sync/15lazy-members.pl
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
